        <div class="prose">
            <p class="lead">Making Exceptions is a podcast about the people who build things. Not the pitch decks or the funding rounds, but the actual work.</p>

            <p>The architecture decisions that shaped a company. The side project that became a product. The moment a technical founder realised they needed to learn how to lead.</p>

            <p>Each episode is a conversation with a technical founder or engineering leader. We dig into their journey from writing code to running teams, making products, and building businesses. The stories are personal, the lessons are practical, and the tone is honest.</p>

            <h2>Format</h2>
            <ul class="format-list">
                <li><span class="mono">Length</span><span>45 to 60 minutes</span></li>
                <li><span class="mono">Structure</span><span>Origin story, what they're building now, the decisions that shaped their path, and a rapid-fire round to close</span></li>
                <li><span class="mono">Medium</span><span>Video and audio</span></li>
                <li><span class="mono">Cadence</span><span>Weekly</span></li>
            </ul>

            <h2>The host</h2>
            <p><a href="https://ejntaylor.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Elliot Taylor</a> is the founder of EJNT Ltd, building products like <a href="https://coderbuds.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coderbuds</a> and <a href="https://bishbashdosh.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BishBashDosh</a>. He's spent over a decade working across engineering, security, and product, and started Making Exceptions to have the conversations he wishes he'd heard earlier in his career.</p>

